Shortcut to start server:
	* python app.py
	* (possible because of this line in app.py):
		* app.run(host="100.117.48.119", port=5000)

In future can experiment with:
	* flask --app app run
	* then either tailscale serve or tailscale funnel the 127 ip over the internet


How to start server for personal usage over tailscale:
	* flask --app flask_backend.py run --host=100.117.48.119

How to start server open to internet:
	* flask --app flask_backend.py run --host=0.0.0.0
